# Java build artifacts. dist/ and classes/ are still written in-tree; the
# generated sources and .jop images are not, as of 2026-09-04 -- they live in
# build/<config>/java/ with the Const.java they are compiled against.
#
# THE ENTRIES BELOW WERE DELETED, NOT MOVED. Ignoring a path that nothing
# should write is how a stale artefact stays invisible: a Const.java left in
# the source tree by a pre-2026-09-04 build is the OTHER configuration's
# constants, and an ignore rule guaranteed nobody would ever see it sitting
# there. It is now untracked and visible, and java/config.mk's CONST_EXCLUDE
# keeps javac from compiling it even if someone leaves one behind.
#
#   java/runtime/src/jop/com/jopdesign/sys/Const.java
#   java/runtime/src/jop/com/jopdesign/sys/.const-preset   (stamp; removed)
#   java/apps/*/*.jop
#   java/apps/*/*.jop.txt  .jop.link.txt  .jop.stats.txt   (JOPizer sidecars)
#   java/tools/dist/          (jars now in build/<config>/java/tools and
#   java/runtime/classes/      build/java/tools; classes under build/ too)
java/apps/*/build/

# ALL generated and transient build products live under build/<config>/ --
# generated HDL, the vendor project, IP, .jop and asm outputs. One directory
# per build CONFIGURATION (preset plus arguments), so two core counts or two
# method-cache geometries cannot overwrite each other's artefacts. The layout
# is parameterised in jop.generate.BuildLayout.
#
# ANCHORED, because a bare `build/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth -- and one of them is SOURCE: java/tools/src/com/jopdesign/build is a
# Java package. Its 31 existing files stayed tracked (git does not un-track what
# it already knows), so the rule was invisible until 2026-09-04, when a NEW file
# added to that package was silently ignored: it built here and the cold clone
# failed to compile, because a clone gets only what is tracked.
#
# The root build tree is already covered by /build/ at the top of this file, and
# the per-app ones by java/apps/*/build/ above, so this rule was redundant as
# well as harmful.

# Kept-aside binaries for a reproduction that is sensitive to code layout: the
# 4-core generational GC failure only reproduces for a particular image, and any
# runtime edit relinks it away (see docs/current-status.md item 1). Not tracked —
# these are build outputs like every other .jop — but not deleted either.
spinalhdl/repro/

# Microcode assembler generated files
# Microcode now lives in build/microcode/<variant>/ (covered by /build/ above).

# Root-level default SpinalHDL output (formal/ad-hoc generation)
/toplevel.v
/*.v_toplevel_*
.cnxerr
qmegawiz_errors_log.txt
fpga/bringup/*/build/
